<title>USA: Advo CFO backs Q1 EPS estimate of $0.25/shr.</title>
<headline>Advo CFO backs Q1 EPS estimate of $0.25/shr.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Advo Inc chief financial officer Lowell Robinson said on Tuesday that Wall Street's consensus estimate for first quarter 1997's earnings per share of $0.25 &quot;appears reasonable at this point.&quot;</p>
<p>Robinson added that several factors that led to a disappointing 1996 have turned around and will benefit 1997, including postal and paper costs and a retail industry that looks as though it is improving. He added that he expects those conditions to continue to improve in 1997.</p>
<p>&quot;We feel extremely bullish (for 1997),&quot; Robinson said.</p>
<p>((--Lisa Marie Pane/New York Equities 212-859-1610))</p>
